3. Training data  --  terms NOT reviewed; see below
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No dataset is redistributed here: data/raw, data/preprocessed and runs/ are all
gitignored. But docs/EarLandmarker_web.onnx IS tracked, and it is a model trained
on those datasets, so whatever terms they carry may reach it.

The 55-point annotation scheme is iBUG's (Zhou & Zaferiou, "Deformable Models of
Ears in-the-wild", FG 2017). The sources are described in README.md as
collectionA (605), collectionB (3,153), AudioEar2D (2,000) and AudioEar3D (112).
Academic ear datasets commonly carry research-only or non-commercial terms.

**Their licences have not been checked against Apache-2.0 redistribution of the
trained weights.** That needs doing before this repository is treated as
commercially usable, and it is independent of item 1.
